# Local-only. SECURITY.md §6 tells an operator to put local secrets in
# .dev.vars; without this line that advice is a trap, because the repo had no
# .gitignore at all before v69 and the file would be committed on the next add.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example

# wrangler's local state and login cache (scratch; never part of a deploy)
.wrangler/

# The desktop app's local session config. It is already outside the repo via
# .git/info/exclude, but that file is one machine's and this one travels: a
# launch config carries binding flags, and since v69.4 a local one carries the
# real DAILY_PINS. A pinned launch board committed here would undo the whole
# reason it was moved out of daily-core.js.
.claude/
